#: ../mergewt/quspect/circuit/circuit.py:docstring of
#: quspect.circuit.circuit.QuantumCircuit:1
msgid "A quantum circuit composed of gates, measurements, and barriers."
msgstr ""

#: ../mergewt/quspect/circuit/circuit.py:docstring of
#: quspect.circuit.circuit.QuantumCircuit:3
msgid ""
"QuantumCircuit is the primary user-facing class. It supports a fluent "
"(method-chaining) API for building circuits gate by gate."
msgstr ""

#: ../mergewt/quspect/circuit/circuit.py:docstring of
#: quspect.circuit.circuit.QuantumCircuit:6
msgid ""
"The number of qubits and classical bits is **dynamically inferred** from the "
"indices used in gates and measurements. There is no need to pre-declare "
"circuit size — the circuit grows automatically as new qubits or classical "
"bits are referenced."
msgstr ""

#: ../mergewt/quspect/circuit/circuit.py:docstring of
#: quspect.circuit.circuit.QuantumCircuit:11
msgid ""
"Gates are added via named methods (e.g., ``.h(0)``) or via the generic "
"``.append(gate, qubits)`` method. Qubit and classical bit indices must be "
"non-negative integers; gaps are allowed (e.g., you can use qubit 3 without "
"first using qubits 0-2)."
msgstr ""

