msgid "Return the number of threads used by the native parallel kernels."
msgstr ""

#: ../mergewt/quspect/native/__init__.py:docstring of
#: quspect.native.get_num_threads:3
msgid ""
"The C++ state-vector kernels (gate application, expectation values, "
"measurement probabilities and collapse), the adjoint-gradient loops and the "
"Ising annealer are parallelized with OpenMP.  Unless :func:`set_num_threads` "
"has been called, the value follows the standard OpenMP defaults, i.e. "
"``OMP_NUM_THREADS`` when it is set, otherwise the number of available "
"cores.  States with fewer than ``2**14`` amplitudes always run single-"
"threaded regardless of this setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../mergewt/quspect/native/__init__.py:docstring of
#: quspect.native.get_num_threads:11
msgid ""
"The current thread count (always ``1`` when the extension was built without "
"OpenMP; see ``capabilities()[\"openmp\"]``)."
msgstr ""

