msgstr ""

#: ../mergewt/quspect/native/__init__.py:docstring of
#: quspect._native_loader.load_core:1
msgid "Return the best native extension module for this CPU, or ``None``."
msgstr ""

#: ../mergewt/quspect/native/__init__.py:docstring of
#: quspect._native_loader.load_core:3
msgid ""
"This is the supported, stable public way to detect whether the QuSpect C++ "
"native core is available; import it as ``from quspect.native import "
"load_core``.  A return value of ``None`` means the native core has not been "
"built (or installed), so native features such "
"as :class:`quspect.native.NativeExecutor` are unavailable. Any non-``None`` "
"return value is the loaded extension module; its name and attributes are "
"implementation details and may change between releases, so treat it only as "
"a truthy \"native core is available\" signal and use the "
"public :mod:`quspect.native` API to interact with it."
msgstr ""

#: ../mergewt/quspect/native/__init__.py:docstring of
#: quspect._native_loader.load_core:13
msgid ""
"The scalar module is imported first.  If it is missing, ``None`` is returned "
"so callers can raise a friendly error or skip native features. When the "
"scalar module reports AVX2 + FMA support via ``cpu_supports_avx2()`` "
"and :data:`DISABLE_AVX2_ENV` is not ``\"1\"``, the AVX2 module is imported "
"instead; if that import fails for any reason the scalar module is used and "
"the failure is logged at DEBUG level."
msgstr ""

#: ../mergewt/quspect/native/__init__.py:docstring of
#: quspect._native_loader.load_core:20
msgid ""
"The result is cached, so the selection happens only once per process. Call "
"``load_core.cache_clear()`` to force a new selection (tests only)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mergewt/quspect/native/__init__.py:docstring of
#: quspect._native_loader.load_core:23
msgid ""
"The loaded extension module (``quspect._core_avx2`` or "
"``quspect._core_scalar``), or ``None`` when the scalar module has not been "
"built."
msgstr ""

#: ../mergewt/quspect/native/__init__.py:docstring of
#: quspect._native_loader.load_core:27
msgid ""
"If the scalar module exists but fails to import, or a     dependency other "
"than the scalar module itself is missing.  Only     a "
"``ModuleNotFoundError`` for :data:`SCALAR_MODULE` is treated as     \"not "
"built\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../mergewt/quspect/native/__init__.py:docstring of
#: quspect.native.set_num_threads:1
msgid "Set the number of threads used by the native parallel kernels."
msgstr ""

#: ../mergewt/quspect/native/__init__.py:docstring of
#: quspect.native.set_num_threads:3
msgid ""
"The setting is process-wide for the loaded native extension and applies to "
"every subsequent native call, from any Python thread.  It takes precedence "
"over ``OMP_NUM_THREADS``.  Results do not depend on the thread count: "
"reductions use a fixed blocking, and seeded sampling produces the same "
"counts for any ``n``.  When the extension was built without OpenMP the value "
"is validated and otherwise ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../mergewt/quspect/native/__init__.py:docstring of
#: quspect.native.set_num_threads:10
msgid "Number of threads; must be at least 1."
msgstr ""

